## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design privacy-preserving, production-grade NLP systems with real-time constraints. It tests understanding of differential privacy, secure aggregation, drift detection, and safe rollout strategies aligned with fintech privacy requirements.

## Key Concepts

- **Real-time inference and latency budgeting**: Designing for low-latency intent detection and PII processing
- **PII detection and redaction**: Identifying and removing sensitive information before storage
- **Privacy-preserving feedback**: Using secure aggregation and differential privacy to safely incorporate user corrections
- **Drift detection and canary rollouts**: Monitoring model performance and safely deploying updates

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: secure gradient aggregation with differential privacy
function aggregateGradients(partialGradients, noiseScale, clipThreshold) {
  // Clip each gradient to prevent individual influence
  const clipped = partialGradients.map(g => clipGradient(g, clipThreshold));

  // Add Gaussian noise for differential privacy
  const privateGradients = clipped.map(g => addNoise(g, noiseScale));

  // Secure aggregation across participants
  return secureAggregate(privateGradients);
}

function clipGradient(gradient, threshold) {
  const norm = Math.sqrt(gradient.reduce((sum, v) => sum + v * v, 0));
  if (norm > threshold) {
    return gradient.map(v => v * (threshold / norm));
  }
  return gradient;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests architecture for privacy-preserving, real-time NLP at the edge in a multilingual enterprise. It emphasizes latency, data governance, explainability, and robust rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Edge + cloud hybrid architecture with privacy budgets (differential privacy or federated learning)
- Lightweight multilingual encoders (distilled models) for on-device inference and PII redaction
- Streaming governance registry for compliance audit trails
- Drift detection on model outputs and safe rollback via versioned model artifacts

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(text) {
  return text
    .replace(/[a-z0-9._%+-]+@[a-z0-9.-]+\.[a-z]{2,}/gi, '[EMAIL_REDACTED]')
    .replace(/\b\d{3}[-.]?\d{3}[-.]?\d{4}\b/g, '[PHONE_REDACTED]')
    .replace(/\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g, '[SSN_REDACTED]');
}

async function processMessage(message, edgeModel) {
  const redacted = redactPII(message.content);
  const prediction = await edgeModel.classify(redacted);

  if (prediction.confidence > 0.9) {
    await registry.log({ 
      violation: prediction.label, 
      redactedContent: redacted,
      timestamp: Date.now() 
    });
  }
  return { flagged: prediction.confidence > 0.9, prediction };
}
```

## Stack Recommendation
- **Edge**: TensorFlow Lite / ONNX Runtime Mobile, distilled XLM-R or mBERT
- **Cloud**: Python backend (FastAPI), Docker/Kubernetes, Redis for streaming
- **Monitoring**: Prometheus + Grafana, MLflow for model versioning
- **Metrics**: P99 latency, precision/recall per language, drift score (KL divergence), privacy budget consumption

